      "text": "UPPER ENDOSCOPIC ULTRASOUND (EUS) REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 5, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Victor Ilunga, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Indication: Pancreatic head mass on CT; tissue diagnosis requested."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "Procedure: As part of this EUS, an EGD was first performed with a standard gastroscope."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "The esophagus, stomach and duodenum to the second portion were normal on the EGD portion."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "The linear echoendoscope was then advanced to the second portion of the duodenum."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "EUS imaging was performed from the esophagus, stomach and duodenum."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "EUS findings: a 24 mm hypoechoic mass in the pancreatic head; common bile duct 9 mm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "EUS-guided fine-needle aspiration of the pancreatic head mass: 22-gauge needle, 3 passes."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "The needle passes were made through the duodenal wall."
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "text": "Impression: 24 mm pancreatic head mass, sampled by EUS-guided fine-needle aspiration."
    }
  ],
